<section class="sy-hero"><div class="sy-w sy-hero-g"><div><p class="sy-ey">Week 1 &middot; Read this first</p><h1>Every course starts with a <mark>syllabus</mark>.</h1><p class="sy-lead">Learn to read course outlines properly, turn them into a week-by-week plan and keep your workload realistic all term.</p><div class="sy-hero-a"><a class="sy-btn" href="#plan">Plan my semester</a><a class="sy-lnk" href="how-to-read-a-syllabus-guide.html">How to read a syllabus &rarr;</a></div>
<dl class="sy-stats"><div><dt>Units in a typical term</dt><dd><span data-count="4">0</span>&ndash;5</dd></div><div><dt>Teaching weeks</dt><dd data-count="12">0</dd></div><div><dt>Study hours per credit</dt><dd>~<span data-count="3">0</span></dd></div></dl></div>
<div class="sy-doc"><div class="sy-doc-p"><div class="sy-doc-h"><b>HIST 204</b><span>Spring term</span></div><p class="sy-doc-t">Course Syllabus</p><ol><li style="--i:0"><span class="sy-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 10l3.5 3.5L15 6"/></svg></span><b>Course overview</b><em>Read first</em></li><li style="--i:1"><span class="sy-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 10l3.5 3.5L15 6"/></svg></span><b>Learning outcomes</b><em>What you will be able to do</em></li><li style="--i:2"><span class="sy-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 10l3.5 3.5L15 6"/></svg></span><b>Assessment</b><em>Essay 40% &middot; Exam 60%</em></li><li style="--i:3"><span class="sy-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 10l3.5 3.5L15 6"/></svg></span><b>Key dates</b><em>Week 6 &middot; Week 12</em></li><li style="--i:4"><span class="sy-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 10l3.5 3.5L15 6"/></svg></span><b>Reading list</b><em>Core and optional</em></li><li style="--i:5"><span class="sy-cb"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 10l3.5 3.5L15 6"/></svg></span><b>Policies</b><em>Late work, attendance</em></li></ol><div class="sy-doc-f"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1692158961562-cb06d93fb63c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=260&q=75" alt="an open weekly planner on a desk" width="520" height="260" fetchpriority="high"></div></div><span class="sy-clip" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sy-note" aria-hidden="true">read me!</span></div></div></section>

<div class="sy-mq mq" aria-hidden="true"><div><span>Learning outcomes</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Assessment</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Key dates</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Reading list</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Office hours</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Late policy</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Rubrics</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Reading week</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Learning outcomes</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Assessment</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Key dates</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Reading list</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Office hours</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Late policy</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Rubrics</span><i>&#10003;</i><span>Reading week</span><i>&#10003;</i></div></div>

<section class="sy-s sy-pl" id="plan"><div class="sy-w"><div class="sy-sh"><p class="sy-ey">Tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Semester planner</h2><p class="sy-p">Enter your term dates and your units. You get a week-by-week chart with teaching weeks, a reading week and the exam period, ready to copy into your calendar.</p></div>
<div class="sy-pl-f"><label>Term starts<input type="date" id="pl-s" value="2027-01-18"></label><label>Term ends<input type="date" id="pl-e" value="2027-05-07"></label><label>Reading week<select id="pl-r"><option value="0">None</option><option value="6" selected>Week 6</option><option value="7">Week 7</option><option value="8">Week 8</option></select></label><label>Exam weeks<select id="pl-x"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option></select></label></div>
<div class="sy-units" id="pl-u"></div><button type="button" class="sy-add" id="pl-a">+ Add a unit</button>
<div class="sy-gantt-w"><div class="sy-gantt" id="pl-g" role="img" aria-label="Weekly semester chart"></div></div><p class="sy-small" id="pl-n" aria-live="polite"></p></div></section>

<section class="sy-s sy-ld" id="load"><div class="sy-w sy-ld-g"><div><p class="sy-ey">Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Workload calculator</h2><p class="sy-p">A common rule of thumb is two to three hours of independent study for every hour in class. Add your credits and commitments to see whether your week actually fits.</p>
<label class="sy-lb" for="ld-c">Credit hours this term <output id="ld-co">15</output></label><input type="range" id="ld-c" min="3" max="24" value="15">
<label class="sy-lb" for="ld-m">Study hours per class hour <output id="ld-mo">2</output></label><input type="range" id="ld-m" min="1" max="3" step=".5" value="2">
<label class="sy-lb" for="ld-w">Paid work per week <output id="ld-wo">10 h</output></label><input type="range" id="ld-w" min="0" max="40" value="10">
<label class="sy-lb" for="ld-s">Sleep per night <output id="ld-so">8 h</output></label><input type="range" id="ld-s" min="6" max="9" step=".5" value="8"></div>
<div class="sy-week"><p class="sy-week-h">Your 168-hour week</p><div class="sy-ring"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 200" id="ld-r" aria-hidden="true"></svg><div><b id="ld-f">0</b><span>free hours</span></div></div><ul class="sy-leg" id="ld-l"></ul><p class="sy-verdict" id="ld-v" aria-live="polite"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="sy-s sy-an"><div class="sy-w sy-an-g"><div class="sy-an-i"><figure class="pxw rv rv-c"><img data-px=".08" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1562217180-021f74991332?auto=format&fit=crop&w=620&h=720&q=75" alt="a planner page with handwritten notes" width="620" height="720" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="sy-hl" aria-hidden="true">highlight this</span></div><div><p class="sy-ey">Anatomy of a syllabus</p><h2 class="rv">Six sections worth reading twice</h2><details class="sy-ac rv" open><summary><i>01</i>Learning outcomes<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>The skills you will be tested on. Every assignment maps back to one of these, so they are the best study guide you will get.</p></details><details class="sy-ac rv"><summary><i>02</i>Assessment weighting<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>How the final grade is split. A 60% exam deserves more of your time than a 10% quiz, however urgent the quiz feels.</p></details><details class="sy-ac rv"><summary><i>03</i>Key dates<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Deadlines, exams and reading weeks. Copy them into your own calendar on the first day of term.</p></details><details class="sy-ac rv"><summary><i>04</i>Reading list<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Core texts are expected; optional ones are for depth. Check which edition is required before buying.</p></details><details class="sy-ac rv"><summary><i>05</i>Office hours<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>When and where staff are available. Students who visit early in term tend to find later questions easier to ask.</p></details><details class="sy-ac rv"><summary><i>06</i>Policies<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Late penalties, extensions, attendance and academic integrity. Read these before you need them.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="sy-s sy-cb2"><div class="sy-w sy-sh"><p class="sy-ey">Around campus</p><h2 class="rv">The term, in snapshots</h2></div><div class="hs sy-hs"><figure class="sy-pc"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1601001435957-74f0958a93fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a stack of pastel notebooks" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Notes</figcaption></figure><figure class="sy-pc"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758270703878-de80505b6714?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="students listening in a lecture" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Lectures</figcaption></figure><figure class="sy-pc"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784359065403-93da31c36115?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="students studying in a library" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Library</figcaption></figure><figure class="sy-pc"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1759852692971-a2abc6799cbd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a smiling student holding books" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Reading</figcaption></figure><figure class="sy-pc"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1614793319738-bde496bbe85e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="an empty classroom with desks" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Seminars</figcaption></figure></div></section>

